<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Monthly Rental</span>
<h1>Interns: Parking and Security Planning in Hanoi | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>An internship&rsquo;s motorbike spends more time standing still than moving, parked overnight outside the accommodation, parked through the working day at the workplace, parked through the evening wherever the social calendar goes, and security on a monthly rental is mostly the story of those standing hours rather than the moving ones. A daily renter hands the machine back before it has learned anyone&rsquo;s routine, but a monthly renter builds a relationship with three or four specific patches of Hanoi pavement, and the quality of those patches decides whether the chapter ends with a clean return walk-around or a difficult conversation. This page sets out the honest habits, the spot-choosing literacy every local rider already has, and the questions worth asking at the counter and at the accommodation, without inventing a single rule the city does not actually publish.</p>
<p>The machine at the centre of this planning comes from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, and the desk there answers what the rental includes for locks and security. Start at the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> hub, anchor the money at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> guide, see the fleet and terms at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, read the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/motorbike-rental-for-expats-hanoi/">motorbike rental for expats</a> guide for the long-stay picture, and browse the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for the street layer the parking sits inside.</p>
